# `WHERE` in capitals after the table, without `|`: a certain fix (DS0153).
mode: syntax
---- query
from t WHERE x > 1 | take 5
---- expected
PROGRAM@0..28
  PIPELINE@0..27
    IDENT@0..4 "from"
    WHITESPACE@4..5 " "
    NAME_REF@5..6
      IDENT@5..6 "t"
    WHITESPACE@6..7 " "
    WHERE_OP@7..18
      IDENT@7..12 "WHERE"
      WHITESPACE@12..13 " "
      BIN_EXPR@13..18
        NAME_REF@13..14
          IDENT@13..14 "x"
        WHITESPACE@14..15 " "
        GT@15..16 ">"
        WHITESPACE@16..17 " "
        LITERAL@17..18
          LONG@17..18 "1"
    WHITESPACE@18..19 " "
    PIPE@19..20 "|"
    WHITESPACE@20..21 " "
    TAKE_OP@21..27
      IDENT@21..25 "take"
      WHITESPACE@25..26 " "
      LITERAL@26..27
        LONG@26..27 "5"
  WHITESPACE@27..28 "\n"

error[DS0153]: `WHERE` is SQL: DataScript pipes the table into an operator
  --> query:1:8
  |
1 | from t WHERE x > 1 | take 5
  |        ^^^^^ expected `|` before this
  |
  = help: pipe the rows into `where`: `| where`

with the machine-applicable fixes applied:
    from t | where x > 1 | take 5
which parses without errors
